# Visual Studio / Rider / VS Code
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sln
*.slnx
*.suo
*.opensdf
*.sdf
*.VC.db
*.VC.opendb

# Unreal generated / regenerable
Binaries/
DerivedDataCache/
Intermediate/
Saved/
Build/
!Build/*/**/*.ini

# The Build/ SOURCE layer collides with the ignore rule above, which targets UE's
# platform build-config directories, not plugin source folders.
#
# These paths were written against the old plugin name and the rename to Airside did
# not carry them over, so the exception stopped matching anything and the whole layer -
# the mesh builder, the network solver, the guideline builder - was silently dropped
# from the repository for four commits. Nothing reported it: the files were on disk and
# the project built, and only `git ls-files` on a directory nobody thought to question
# would have shown it. `main` would not have compiled from a fresh clone.
#
# Matched by DIRECTORY NAME rather than by full path, so the next rename cannot repeat
# this. Un-ignoring a directory needs the pattern that re-admits its contents too - git
# never descends into an excluded directory, so `!.../Build/` alone re-admits nothing.
!**/Source/**/Build/
!**/Source/**/Build/**

# Compiled source
*.dll
*.exe
*.lib
*.pdb
*.obj
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.app
*.ipa
